answer.worked:
In the base of the prism, the horizontal components of $ML$ are $11 - 3 = 8$ cm and $18 - 3 = 15$ cm.
$$\begin{align*}
ML &= \sqrt{8^2 + 15^2} \\
&= \sqrt{64 + 225} \\
&= 17 \text{ cm}
\end{align*}$$
Using the right-angled triangle with angle $30^\circ$:
$$\begin{align*}
\tan 30^\circ &= \frac{h}{17} \\
h &= 17\tan 30^\circ \\
&= \frac{17\sqrt{3}}{3} \text{ cm}
\end{align*}$$
The answer is (B).

